    {
      "id": "2e0725e1-18e2-483e-b287-4bdbdf632d5d",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -512,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Automate incident postmortems with AI, Google Sheets, Discord and Gmail\n\n### How it works\n\n1. A team member submits an incident report through the hosted form (what happened, severity, impacted service, suspected cause).\n2. The workflow validates the report, then an AI agent drafts a structured postmortem with overview, timeline, root cause, impact, and action items.\n3. The postmortem is saved to Google Sheets, action items are tracked in their own sheet, and stakeholders get the full draft by email.\n4. High or critical incidents trigger an urgent alert on Discord, while other incidents get a digest post.\n5. Every Monday the workflow reviews open action items, emails owners about overdue items, alerts the team on Discord, and sends a weekly digest.\n\n### Setup\n\n- Connect Google Sheets, Gmail, Discord, and OpenAI credentials.\n- Create a spreadsheet with Postmortems and ActionItems sheets, then update the two Google Sheets nodes.\n- Update the Discord channel and the stakeholder email addresses in the Gmail nodes.\n\n### Customization\n\n- Change the form fields, the AI prompt, the severity thresholds, or the weekly schedule to match your process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
